### Golang Polyglot

<hr style="width:100%;border-bottom:3px solid black;">

{{macros.admonition("warning", "Non-core", "This is the non-core `polyglot.golang.cmk` plugin, and it needs a docker daemon (the Go toolchain runs in a container; nothing is installed on the host).")}}

`polyglot.golang.cmk` lets you embed **inline Go** in a `compose.mk`/CMK program: it cross-builds the
source in a dockerized Go toolchain, caches the resulting binary per-host, and execs it.  No Go
install is required on the host, and a clean (cache-hit) run just execs the cached binary.

```make
$(call include.plugins, polyglot.golang.cmk)
```

#### How it works
<hr style="width:100%;border-bottom:3px solid black;">

The Go source and `go.mod` are provided as CMK **block-refs** (defines).  On first use the plugin:

1. cross-compiles for the host (`GOOS`/`GOARCH` auto-detected, env-overridable) inside the toolchain
   image, then chowns the output back to the host UID;
2. caches the binary at `${CMK_XDG_CACHE}/<hash>/<name>`, keyed by a checksum of the **source + module**
   content -- so editing either triggers a clean rebuild, and an unchanged program is a cache HIT;
3. execs it, forwarding any arguments.

#### Public surface
<hr style="width:100%;border-bottom:3px solid black;">

| Symbol | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `declare.polyglot.golang(namespace=<ns> src= mod= ..)` | generate a `<ns>` (run) target and a `<ns>/%` (run with the stem as argv) target |
| `polyglot.golang.lambda(src= mod= [name=] [base=] [args=])` | build-if-needed, then exec |
| `polyglot.golang.ensure(<src>,<mod>,<name>,<base>)` | build-if-absent (a cache HIT just logs) |
| `polyglot.golang.base` | the toolchain image (default `golang:1.24-bookworm`, overridable) |

#### Example
<hr style="width:100%;border-bottom:3px solid black;">

Declare a namespace over an inline Go program, then call it like any other target -- the stem after the
slash is passed through as argv:

```make
$(call include.plugins, polyglot.golang.cmk)
$(call declare.polyglot.golang, namespace=golang src=main.go mod=go.mod)

__main__: golang golang/hello

define main.go
package main
import ( "fmt"; "os" )
func main(){ if len(os.Args)>1 { fmt.Println("hi", os.Args[1]) } else { fmt.Println("hi") } }
endef

define go.mod
module poly
go 1.24
endef
```

See `demos/cmk/golang-lambda.cmk` in the source tree for a worked example.

